conf, flow: reset over the control socket, and a status reply

Two additions to the configuration protocol (pesto), for a caller that keeps
one pasta and its namespace and lends them to one guest after another.

- A client may send PESTO_RESET (0xff) in place of a pif id before its
  tables. passt then closes every flow (TCP, spliced TCP, UDP, ping) without
  sending anything to the tap, and puts back the guest MAC and the guest
  addresses it had before any traffic (guest_mac, ip4.addr_seen,
  ip6.addr_seen, ip6.addr_ll_seen), which it otherwise learns from the
  guest's frames. Until now the only way to drop that state was to restart
  pasta, which costs a TAP detach and attach under the host's rtnl_mutex.
  The flows are closed in flow_defer_handler(), at the end of the epoll
  cycle the request arrived in, because an event of the same batch may still
  name one of them.
- After applying a client's tables passt answers with one status byte before
  it closes the connection: bit 0 (PESTO_STATUS_LISTEN_FAILED) says a rule
  could not be bound. fwd_listen_switch() returns that instead of only
  logging it. For a reset the byte is sent once the flows are closed. A
  client that does not read it (pesto) is not affected.

Carried by fcvm for its pooled namespaces. Not submitted upstream yet.

